diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..15d393e 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -159,3 +159,13 @@ __Response:__
 ```
 
 `request` and `response` can be `null` for deliveries that have not started yet or are still in progress. The delivery request headers omit the `X-Webhook-Signature` header.
+
+## Delivery behaviour
+
+When something happens on a board, every active webhook on that board that is subscribed to the action receives a `POST` with the event as a JSON payload. The payload is signed with the webhook's `signing_secret` using `HMAC-SHA256` and sent in the `X-Webhook-Signature` header, alongside the time of the event in `X-Webhook-Timestamp`.
+
+Each event is delivered exactly once: deliveries are never retried. Whatever happens is kept in the delivery log, where `state` is one of `pending`, `in_progress`, `completed`, or `errored`, and `response` holds the response `code` of the receiver or the `error` that prevented the delivery.
+
+Deliveries are kept for a week, after which they are cleaned up.
+
+A receiver that keeps failing — ten deliveries in a row within an hour — gets the webhook deactivated. It has to be reactivated to receive deliveries again.
